std/binary returns Err "binary: read past end" when a fixed-width read runs past the end. This occurs because the read operation attempts to access memory beyond the allocated buffer size, triggering the error condition defined in the binary module.

```sol
// Example: Attempting to read 4 bytes from a 2-byte buffer
let buf = bytes([1, 2]);
let result = binary.read(buf, 4);
// result will be Err "binary: read past end"
```

