Duplicate keys are retained in the order of their first appearance. The library does not raise an error or remove duplicates; instead, it preserves the initial sequence of identical keys within the object structure.

```sol
// Example: Duplicate keys are kept in first-appearance order
let obj = {
  name: "Alice",
  age: 30,
  name: "Alice", // Duplicate key retained
  city: "NYC"
}
```
